{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>And the fortress.</b> Like 'walls of,' concerning Moab." "<b>He has laid low, brought low.</b> Without a conjunction vav, like כרע שכב נפל (Judges 5:27). The sense of 'he has laid low' is that he had already laid low when Sennacherib came."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {0 "The kaph of חומותי is comparative, taken in opposition to Moab."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:55:09.539009283Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}